# Allowlist for scripts/forbidden_words.py, one exception per line.
#
#   <path glob> | <rule id, matched text or *> | <reason>
#
# * The glob is matched against the path from the repository root; "*" also crosses folders.
# * The term is a rule id (python3 scripts/forbidden_words.py --list-rules), the exact matched
#   text (for example one store domain), "placeholder", "template-hint", "email" or "*" (any rule
#   except "email"). Terms from the private list (--extra-terms) can never be excused.
# * "@name" as the path covers the name check (repository, package and README title names).
# * Every entry needs a reason. Scope entries to data or UI files, or to the
#   one domain the project really links to. A funding file can never be allowlisted.
# * Unused entries are reported as warnings; delete them.

scripts/forbidden_words.py | * | the check's own rule list, its documentation and the usage examples
tests/test_forbidden_words.py | * | test sentences that must trigger the rules
tests/test_check_pr_title.py | * | test titles that must be rejected for their wording
scripts/set_byline.py | placeholder | prints the names of the placeholders to fill again after a brand swap
LICENSE | sell | the licence grants the right to "sell copies" of the software
assets/fonts/OFL.txt | sell | the unchanged SIL Open Font License text of the bundled Sora font (it forbids selling the font by itself)
assets/fonts/OFL.txt | scripts.sil.org | the licence's own reference URL in the unchanged OFL text
island/vite.config.js | affiliates | React's copyright holder line ("Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates"), kept verbatim in the bundle banner as MIT requires
gallery/vite.config.js | affiliates | React's copyright holder line ("Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates"), kept verbatim in the gallery bundle banner as MIT requires
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md | affiliates | React's copyright holder line ("Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates") in the licence notice
package-lock.json | funding | npm lockfile: the "funding" metadata fields of third-party packages (generated by npm, not our text)
package-lock.json | funding-platform | npm lockfile: third-party packages' own funding URLs (generated by npm, not our text)
package-lock.json | sponsor | npm lockfile: third-party packages' own sponsor URLs (generated by npm, not our text)
